<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Bacillus subtilis Turing wavenumber at 16 µm (Holocene detail scale) (Bacillus subtilis)",
        "Bacillus subtilis Turing wavenumber at 16 µm (Holocene detail scale) faithfully reproduces Bacillus subtilis morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0.py, docs/media/bacillus_subtilis_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Bacillus subtilis specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/bacillus_subtilis_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Bacillus subtilis" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim that any cited paper measured a 16 µm pigment stripe in B. subtilis.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the faint bulk field in pass 1 has reached a nonlinear Turing pattern.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: A kinematic circular front with m=round(2 pi R / 16 µm)=72 at R=183.3 µm, which is a reconstruction, not a measured radius.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics a=0.084, b=0.916, diffusion ratio 9.20, calibrated so argmax sigma_plus is 16.02 µm.",
        "reported_in_source: Kawasaki 1997, Golding 1998, and Ben-Jacob 2000 model Bacillus subtilis colony branches with reaction-diffusion at colony scale.",
        "reported_in_source: The Korinna 2019 micrograph is an eye-shaped B. subtilis colony and carries no scale bar.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 selects a finite critical wavenumber from a two-species reaction-diffusion system.",
        "transfer_boundary: Colony-scale branching papers are used as the organism's reaction-diffusion context. They are not a measurement of a 16 µm wavelength." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/bacillus_subtilis_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; output: docs/media/bacillus_subtilis_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; organism: Bacillus subtilis; environment: python 3.12; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 selects a finite critical wavenumber from a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Kawasaki 1997, Golding 1998, and Ben-Jacob 2000 model Bacillus subtilis colony branches with reaction-diffusion at colony scale. | The Korinna 2019 micrograph is an eye-shaped B. subtilis colony and carries no scale bar.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics a=0.084, b=0.916, diffusion ratio 9.20, calibrated so argmax sigma_plus is 16.02 µm. | A kinematic circular front with m=round(2 pi R / 16 µm)=72 at R=183.3 µm, which is a reconstruction, not a measured radius.; transfer_boundary: Colony-scale branching papers are used as the organism's reaction-diffusion context. They are not a measurement of a 16 µm wavelength.; does_not_claim: Does not claim that any cited paper measured a 16 µm pigment stripe in B. subtilis. | Does not claim the faint bulk field in pass 1 has reached a nonlinear Turing pattern.]; other sources: Eye shaped Bacillus subtilis bacteria colony under the microscope <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eye_shaped_Bacillus_subtilis_bacteria_colony_under_the_microscope.jpg>; phenomenon_size: 5.4 cm (0.05445 m, log10=-1.264 m, tier=7_organism_cm); species_scale_ladder (1 runs from 5.4 cm to 5.4 cm): 5.4 cm:bacillus-biofilm-wrinkling" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1997.0462>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0378-4371(98)00345-8>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/000187300405228>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-10>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-8>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-delphi10000-bacillus-subtilis-turing-wavelength-s0-9> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Reaction-Diffusion & Turing Dispersion" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 8.44e-01 .

